            <ArticleTitle>Nickel exposure from keys: a Brazilian issue.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>734-735</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0365-05962017000500734</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/abd1806-4841.20175754</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Keys are a significant source of exposure to metal allergens and can be a relevant problem for nickel-allergic individuals. This study aimed to perform nickel and cobalt spot testing among the 5 most common Brazilian brands of keys. Among the tested keys, 100% showed positive result to nickel spot test, 83,3% presented strong positive reaction. 50% exhibited cobalt release as well. Nickel release from keys is very common in our country and may cause a negative impact on sensitized individual's quality of life. Study's results highlight the importance of establishing directives to regulate nickel release in Brazil.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
